enchilada: MSS stage 8 (mss=8): WLFW QMI client up to WLAN mission mode (Wi-Fi round 4)

mss=8 = mss=7 plus the WLFW client of Linux v6.12 ath10k qmi.c / qmi_wlfw_v01.c for WCN3990,
ported from topaz 0122/0124 and checked against ath10k for SDM845: when the modem announces
service 0x45 v1, ind_register (fw_ready, msa_ready, client id 0x4b4e454c) -> host_cap with the
8-bit daemon_support of qcom,snoc-host-cap-8bit-quirk (mainline sdm845-oneplus-common) ->
msa_info for wlan_msa_mem 0x8df00000 + 1 MiB (our DT's wlan_fw_region) -> 20 ms -> each
returned region checked as ath10k does and assigned HLOS -> {MSS_MSA, WLAN 0x18, WLAN_CE 0x19
unless secure} RW (ath10k_qmi_map_msa_permission) -> msa_ready -> cap (chip, family, board, soc,
fw version and build logged; retried up to 5 times as topaz 0124) -> on the MSA_READY indication
the board file in 6144-byte segments (a failure on the last one tolerated, as ath10k does) ->
cal_report -> on FW_READY wlan_cfg with snoc.c's CE, service (zero entry included) and shadow
tables -> wlan_mode mission; wlan_mode off at the end of the 120 s watch. Board file: ath10k
loads board-2.bin "bus=snoc,qmi-board-id=ff,qmi-chip-id=30214,variant=oneplus_sdm845" for this
phone, which is byte for byte modem_a's bdwlan.bin (sha256 a46790bc...), so it is read from
modem_a through mss_tftp[] and checked by crc32; other ids fall back to the vendor's cnss name and
say so. MSA regions return to HLOS RW (ath10k_qmi_remove_msa_permission) when the WLFW service
goes away, after a failed msa_ready/cap, or in the stop path after the Q6 reset. mss_assign
learns the WLAN VMIDs, an HLOS RW reclaim and a third destination entry (extended arguments then
at +0x100; one- and two-destination calls are laid out exactly as before). No WLAN register is
touched; mss<=7 behave as before.

